cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenSuperSampling (OSS) in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenSuperSampling: Open, Cross-Vendor Real-Time Game Super-Resolution and Frame Extrapolation"
authors:
  - family-names: Conway
    given-names: Cash
    affiliation: "OpenSuperSampling Project"
type: software
version: "0.2.0-dev"
date-released: 2026-04-29
url: "https://github.com/cashcon57/open-supersampling"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cashcon57/open-supersampling"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - super-resolution
  - real-time-rendering
  - gaussian-splatting
  - temporal-super-resolution
  - frame-extrapolation
  - game-engine
  - open-source
  - cross-vendor
abstract: >-
  OpenSuperSampling is a pre-alpha open-source real-time game super-resolution
  and frame-extrapolation system targeting cross-vendor deployment via custom
  per-GPU-vendor kernels (CUDA, HIP, Metal, Level Zero, Vulkan compute). The
  v6 architecture is covariance-resampled online Gaussian-temporal SR with a
  HAT spatial backbone, persistent Gaussian canvas with engine-motion-vector
  analytical sub-pixel warp, cross-attention pixel-Gaussian fusion, and
  Spatial-Temporal Variation Score pruning. Frame extrapolation is provided
  as a byproduct of alpha-conditioned canvas rendering at fractional time
  positions. Game integration via DLL-shim drop-in compatible with any
  DLSS/FSR/XeSS-supporting title — no developer cooperation required.
